        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:53:39Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): generic ISO wire EDM post - RS-274 motion, every EDM code from the machine's edm.codes\n\nassets/posts/wire-iso.cps (\"Generic ISO Wire EDM\") posts the 2-axis Wire\nContour: G0 to the start hole, AWT thread (or M00 for the operator),\ncondition select and compensation cancel from .mch edm.codes, the\nwire-centre path in G1/G2/G3 X Y with no F, then wire cut and tip\ndisposal. A missing required code refuses by name (\"machine <m> states\nno edm.codes.<x>\"); a non-wire_edm machine is refused by name.\n\n- post: Machine.edm_codes parsed from edm.codes (edm_codes.rs); the\n  mirror and script_props expose machine.kind and machine.edm for EDM\n  kinds; the engine refuses PARAM EdmCondition through a script without\n  the wireEdm manifest flag.\n- app: posting_wire streams the op's section (EdmCondition, WireSide);\n  WIRE_POSTS, post_serves and default_post_for serve wire EDMs.\n- tests: wire_post.rs with a synthetic fixture (fictional FX- codes) and\n  the golden nc/wire-iso/wire_contour_punch.nc.\n\nNot exercised on a real EDM control (#290 D10).\n\nFixes #533\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
